  "executive_summary": "The analysis covered 311 tables and 1654 query patterns across Aurora PostgreSQL, DynamoDB, DocumentDB and OpenSearch. OpenSearch was eliminated because its only 2 queries are low-frequency `to_tsvector` expressions that Aurora PostgreSQL serves natively with its built-in full-text search. Aurora PostgreSQL carries the relational and text-search work, DynamoDB serves key-based lookups and DocumentDB serves document-shaped queries, and each table's copies in other engines are kept current by CDC from its source of truth.",
  "executive_summary_source": "llm",
